When specified, is used to create a custom section header parser regexp. Must contain a match group named 'label' (written as (?<label>.+)) that encapsulates the section header. Optionally can include another match group named 'separator'. To match multi-line headers like: // ========== // My Section // ========== Use a pattern like: ^={3,}
^// *(?<label>[^
]*?)
^={3,}$
